{
  "mn92:0.1": "Middle Discourses 92 ",
  "mn92:0.2": "With Sela ",
  "mn92:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn92:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was wandering together with a large Saṅgha of 1,250 mendicants in the land of the Aṅguttarāpans when he arrived at a town of theirs named Āpaṇa. ",
  "mn92:2.1": "The matted-hair ascetic Keṇiya heard: ",
  "mn92:2.2": "“It seems the ascetic Gotama—a Sakyan, gone forth from a Sakyan family—has arrived at Āpaṇa, together with a large Saṅgha of 1,250 mendicants. ",
  "mn92:2.3": "He has this good reputation: ",
  "mn92:2.4": "‘That Blessed One is perfected, a fully awakened Buddha, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, holy, knower of the world, supreme guide for those fit for training, teacher of gods and humans, awakened, blessed.’ ",
  "mn92:2.5": "He has realized with his own insight this world—with its gods, Māras, and divinities, this population with its ascetics and brahmins, gods and humans—and he makes it known to others. ",
  "mn92:2.6": "He proclaims a teaching that’s good in the beginning, good in the middle, and good in the end, meaningful and well-phrased. And he reveals a spiritual practice that’s entirely full and pure. ",
  "mn92:2.7": "It’s good to see such perfected ones.” ",
  "mn92:3.1": "So Keṇiya approached the Buddha and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "mn92:3.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side. ",
  "mn92:3.3": "The Buddha educated, encouraged, fired up, and i